<title>BELGIUM: Belgian September unemployment 14.2 pct - minister.</title>
<headline>Belgian September unemployment 14.2 pct - minister.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian Employment Minister Miet Smet said in a statement that Belgium's unemployment rate fell to 14.2 percent in September, compared with 14.5 percent in August.</p>
<p>There were 474,677 people claiming benefits, down 19,252 or 3.9 percent from August, the minister said.</p>
<p>According to the seasonally-adjusted calculation used by the European Union the rate was an unchanged 9.7 percent.</p>
<p>Belgium's National Employment Office is due to publish the official September unemployment data on Thursday.</p>
